From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:52:44 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Video on Windows 10 Mobile: decode waited for before
 conversion, a DXVA probe, bounded decoder quirks

At feature level 9_3 the decoder and the compositor share one device and
nothing is shared between them. The wait after the video processor's
conversion fixed old frames once, but the decode into the NV12 surface the
conversion reads had no wait at all, and the surface then still held a frame
from several cycles before: old frames flashing up on a Lumia 650.
media.wmf.gecko-w10m.frame-sync 2 (the default) also waits for the decode.

Once per process the first hardware H.264 decoder asks the GPU what it can
decode (profiles, NV12, sizes up to the first refused one) and notes it;
mediaCapabilities.decodingInfo for H.264 is answered from that instead of a
decoder built per query, and page queries say no at or above a size the
decoder refused. Frames that come out of order are dropped; after three, low
latency mode is left off for later decoders. Unexpected ProcessOutput
failures can be retried (off by default). Frames carry their number for the
compositor's notes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
